-- Round 012-pre (2026-08-22) — P6 STAGE 1 (the CONVERTER, §10.3) pre-registered
-- expectations, committed BEFORE any implementation (mirrors the
-- round-005/007/009/010/011-pre precedent: this file is its OWN commit ahead of
-- the implementation commit, so the pre-registration ordering is git-auditable).
-- Assert-only, never retract. round-012.rofl carries actuals, separate commit.
--
-- Base commit at pre-registration: 6b7ac6bc (R-8 OQ acks on top of the
-- round-011/P5 chain fa40b361..db71f31b). Worktree clean at registration.
--
-- ══ STAGE SPLIT (the P6 boundary, registered here so the round cannot creep) ══
--
-- STAGE 1 (THIS round) = the converter binary `rofl-convert` (fifth [[bin]] in
-- packages/rfdb-server/Cargo.toml — today exactly four, Cargo.toml:107-121,
-- matching doc §10.3 «четыре бинаря»), standalone, no network, no derive
-- engine, PLUS its own minimal fact-segment WRITER and verification READER
-- (FactStore read subset over the new layout: live fact enumeration,
-- canonical_state_sha, C1 record reassembly). Rationale: §10.3 line ~1680 «он
-- обязан уметь работать без сети и без движка вывода» makes the converter's
-- acceptance self-contained — C1 (round-trip) and C7 (report) are verifiable
-- with only the converter's own reader; nothing in §10.3's six duties requires
-- the ENGINE to read the output. The reader is not throwaway: it is the seed of
-- the stage-2 native facts backend (§8 rfdb-store-lsm fact side).
--
-- STAGE 2 (NEXT round, contract sketched, explicitly NOT here — it is NOT
-- bounded to one workflow; it touches wire+HTTP+cypher+datalog+graph-view
-- consumers, §4.1):
--   (a) engine routing switch §5.2 (blake3_u64(subject) % shard_count in the
--       ENGINE write path; MVCC conflict key (perspective,predicate,subject));
--   (b) opening SegmentType/manifest so MultiShardStore/ManifestStore read
--       fact segments (types.rs:84-96 from_u8 rejects any third variant today
--       — WHY the current engine cannot read the converted store, by code);
--   (c) node_view §3.3 materialized Composite + the four http_server.rs
--       full-scan consumers;
--   (d) legacy read paths (cypher/, datalog five-way reverse_attr_lookup,
--       graph view) onto FactStore;
--   (e) acceptance criteria C2 (six enrichers back on BatchHandle.commit),
--       C3-full (compaction ⊕-invariance incl. the two-author Count gate —
--       stage 1 ships NO compaction), C4 (P8 backends), C5 (v0 corpus 29
--       tests), C6 (pack-phase perf fence 56.2/74 s), C8 (crash gate on
--       supersession — §10.4 pins it to P7).
--
-- ══ THE SIX §10.3 DUTIES AS IMPLEMENTED-INTENT (registered before code) ══
--
-- D1 INPUT READ-ONLY. Open /tmp/rofl-p2-real-base/graph.rfdb through the
--    existing facts seam (LsmFactStore::open, facts/lsm.rs:204) AFTER a
--    preflight that (i) ABORTS if <input>/LOCK exists (the differential
--    precedent facts/differential.rs:1678 REMOVES LOCK — the converter must
--    never mutate the input, so it aborts instead), and (ii) reads current.json
--    version and manifest_index.json latest_version directly and ABORTS on
--    mismatch — because ManifestStore::open otherwise calls rebuild_index
--    (manifest.rs:945) which PERSISTS manifest_index.json into the input
--    (atomic_write_json, manifest.rs ~:2355). Verified on the round's input:
--    current.json version = 171 == manifest_index.json latest_version = 171,
--    so the guarded path is never taken on a healthy base. Output directory
--    creation FAILS if the directory exists. Input recursive sha256 + size
--    (du -sb = 567,405,250 B) asserted unchanged after every run; lsof probe
--    before/after each timed run.
-- D2 DECOMPOSITION per §6.2, VARIANT A (Q8 ack below) with A″ span-collapse
--    (Q6 ack below). Node record → sid/2, type/2, name/2, file/2 (empty-string
--    columns omit the fact, counter in report; content_hash MEASURED 0/503,443
--    → NO content_hash predicate; a nonzero content_hash in an input is
--    outside the measured envelope and is a typed ABORT, not silent loss),
--    one fact per non-reserved metadata key. Edge record → edge_type-as-
--    predicate binary fact (Id src, Id dst); edge-metadata facts keyed by the
--    edge fid EID = fid("main", <EDGE_TYPE>, [Id(src), Id(dst)]) — computed,
--    never materialized as edge_of/3 (variant A). Every predicate declared in
--    the P1 PredicateCatalog (derive/catalog.rs declare()); reverse runs per
--    the §6.3 normative matrix ONLY: edge preds, type, file, name, sid = YES;
--    metadata = NO; plus the three step-4 Adjacency preds (Adjacency declares
--    both runs by §3.1 definition); span/5 = NO reverse (§6.3 A″: span facts
--    have no reverse run).
-- D3 ASSERTION FIELDS per §10.1: author ← interned _source (sha256-hex authors
--    carried AS-IS and REGISTERED as pollution: distinct hex-author count +
--    affected assertion count in the report — Q4/P2 policy, facts/lsm.rs:14-16);
--    tick ← _generation (JSON number or numeric string, the provenance()
--    tolerance at facts/lsm.rs:1003); perspective = main for ALL converted
--    facts + ONE explicit manifest field recording that ruling (§10.1:
--    perspective is unrecoverable — recorded, not implied). Missing _source →
--    author $legacy; missing _generation → tick 0; exact counters in report.
-- D4 RETYPING: metadata keys source_node / handler_function_id / anchorCall
--    with JSON-string values parsing as decimal u128 → Value::Id; the three
--    predicates declared PhysStrategy::Adjacency. Values under those keys NOT
--    parsing as decimal u128 stay as-is and are counted (retype_misses,
--    expected 0). No blanket retyping of decimal strings under other keys.
-- D5 FUNCTIONAL RESOLUTION under R-1a over the CONVERTED vocabulary, with
--    conflict/5 emitted DURABLY into perspective `audit` in the output store
--    (OQ-4 ack lands here). Order (identical to P5 resolve_functional_with,
--    facts/lsm.rs:2037): max tick → seeded author_priority pair
--    (haskell-runtime-globals > haskell-local-refs; applies IFF every
--    max-tick survivor's author is listed and not all one rank) → author
--    canon-order (shortlex, cmp_len_prefixed — NOT plain str::cmp) → min fid.
--    Tuple per OQ-1/OQ-2: [Id(subject), Str(predicate NAME), Id(winner_fid),
--    Id(loser_fid), Int(winner tick)]. LOSERS STAY LIVE (Q10 ack below).
--    RECORDED DEVIATION DEV-P6-1: the spec text says «reusing
--    LsmFactStore::resolve_functional»; that function is bound to the base-five
--    node/type RECORD projection and cannot resolve the converted vocabulary's
--    file/name/sid predicates (OQ-5's attr/3 deferral is WHY). The converter
--    implements the SAME R-1a order over decomposed facts, and CROSS-CHECKS
--    its `type` winners against LsmFactStore::resolve_functional on every
--    multi-record subject (winner value+author+tick must agree) — the return-
--    channel consumption the spec intends, without pretending the base-five
--    resolver speaks the 141-predicate vocabulary.
-- D6 canonical_state_sha of the NEW base per §9.1/§9.2, computed by the
--    converter's own reader: BLAKE3("ROFL-STATE-v1\n" ⧺ varint(max live tick)
--    ⧺ live facts in canon order (perspective NAME, predicate NAME, tuple
--    canon bytes) ⧺ per fact varint(|assertions|) ⧺ assertions sorted by
--    (author, tick) as u32(author) ⧺ u64(tick) ⧺ u16(semiring) ⧺
--    len-prefixed(tag)). PINNED CALL: the u32 author component is the OUTPUT
--    author-table id = the author name's rank in the canonical shortlex-sorted
--    author table (process-invariant by construction; the lsm precedent's
--    byte-sorted live-author rank is a DIFFERENT pinned choice for a DIFFERENT
--    fact model — no cross-model sha equality is claimed, see NON-CLAIMS).
--    Plus the four §9.4 metrics in the report.
--
-- ══ OPEN-QUESTION ACKS (delegation active, OWNER-RULINGS header) ══
--
-- Q1 ACK  — output container: NEW header magic, NEW module
--           facts/convert/segment.rs; storage_v2 UNTOUCHED (SegmentType NOT
--           extended — that opening is stage 2's engine change; zero
--           storage_v2 diff is also the perf-proxy exemption proof). Accepted
--           risk: stage 2 either adopts this header or re-encodes once.
-- Q2 ACK  — catalog persisted IN rofl_manifest.json (single-version, written
--           atomically LAST via temp+rename), version-tagged
--           ("rofl-facts-v1") so stage 2 can evolve it. First-ever catalog
--           persistence; the serde schema is a format commitment.
-- Q3 ACK  — verification path = the converter's own reader ONLY. Explicitly
--           NOT claimed: any engine query over the converted store.
-- Q4 ACK  — $legacy + sha256-hex authors carried as-is, pollution registered.
-- Q5 ACK  — determinism sources eliminated by: interned ids
--           (predicate/author/perspective) assigned AFTER full vocabulary
--           collection in canonical SHORTLEX name order; sorted collections on
--           every output path (no HashMap iteration order reaches output);
--           NO wall-clock timestamps anywhere in the output (the
