-- ══ MINIMAL FORMAT CALLS (Q1/Q2 details, each a recorded commitment) ══
--
-- F1 Segment file family: shards/shard_{:04}/pred_{pid:06}_{fwd|rev}.seg —
--    one file per (shard, predicate, run-direction) with rows present.
--    Columnar: header (magic "ROFLSEG1", format u32=1, predicate id u32,
--    direction u8, arity u8, row count u32), per-segment string table
--    (sorted unique strings, Str cells reference it by u32 index — the
--    string_table.rs convention generalized), value columns cell-encoded
--    (canon tag byte + fixed payload; Term/BigInt varint-len canon bytes),
--    assertion columns per row: perspective u32, author u32, tick u64,
--    semiring u16, varint-len tag bytes, tx_created u64, tx_invalidated u64
--    (variant A row shape, §6.3; A′ RLE is a stage-2+ optimization, not a
--    requirement). Physical row = ONE ASSERTION (a 2-assertion fact = 2
--    adjacent rows) — §9.4 `rows` therefore counts assertion-rows × runs.
--    Rows born sorted by the run's declared key_cols in §9.2 canon value
--    order (then full-tuple canon bytes, then (author,tick)); no L0, no
--    tombstones — stage 1 supersedes nothing. Bloom over the leading key
--    column ONLY when it is Id-typed (u128 split into two u64 halves — the
--    bloom.rs probe convention), stored in-file, params in the descriptor;
--    zone map = min/max canon-bytes of the leading key column per segment
--    (descriptor fields). The reader does not NEED bloom/zone (full-scan
--    verification); they are the §3.2 conventions carried into the format.
-- F2 Routing: shard = blake3_u64(canon_bytes(leading key column value)) %
--    shard_count, where blake3_u64 = first 8 LE bytes of BLAKE3; the REVERSE
--    run routes by ITS OWN leading column (c1) — each run is prefix-probeable
--    within one shard by construction.
-- F3 rofl_manifest.json (root, atomic-last): format tag; shard_count; FULL
--    catalog (name, arity, strategy, cardinality, temporal, semiring,
--    key_cols, reverse, author_priority AS NAMES, stats{live_facts,
--    live_asserts; distinct/max_fanout/updated_at_tx = 0 sentinel «not
--    computed» — compaction-maintained stats are stage-2+, §3.1});
--    author table + perspective table in canonical shortlex order (id =
--    position); per-segment descriptors (pred id, shard, direction,
--    row_count, byte_len, zone min/max, bloom params, content sha256);
--    provenance block (input path, input recursive sha256, input manifest
--    version 171, converter git SHA); the explicit perspective=main ruling
--    field (D3); canonical_state_sha. NO timestamps.
-- F4 Report: conversion-report.json OUTSIDE the store dir (CLI --report).
--    The report is NOT part of the byte-identity gate (it carries wallclock);
--    the OUTPUT DIRECTORY is. The report carries the output dir's recursive
--    sha256 so the two runs are comparable by their own evidence.
-- F5 New direct dependency: sha2 = "0.10" (already in Cargo.lock at 0.10.9 as
--    a transitive dep — no lockfile version movement) for in-process sha256
--    (input immutability + segment content shas). BLAKE3 stays the identity
--    hash; sha256 is the external-evidence hash (matches sha256sum).
--
-- ══ CONVERSION SEMANTICS CALLS (registered before code) ══
--
-- S1 Record enumeration = iter_node_versions_at / iter_edge_versions_at over
--    one pinned snapshot (manifest-descriptor-driven, newest-first — the
--    round-011 re-pin's O(base) enumeration precedent). Reserved
--    $supersedes-type records in the input are a typed ABORT (stage 1
--    converts record-model bases; the real base has none).
-- S2 Input dedup: (i) exact-duplicate records (all fields equal) collapse
--    newest-first, counted (node/edge exact_duplicates); (ii) NON-identical
--    records sharing (identity key, author, tick) — node key = id, edge key =
--    (src,dst,edge_type) — keep NEWEST, drop+count (node/edge
--    shadowed_dropped, EXPECTED 0 on the real base; dropped records are
--    excluded from the C1 input multiset with the counter as the explanation
--    — the record model itself cannot distinguish same-aid re-writes, M1/P7
--    class). Records sharing identity but DIFFERING in (author, tick) are
--    ALL kept — they are distinct assertions (the 39 measured pairs).
-- S3 Assertion dedup by aid (fid, author, tick): the same fact asserted by
--    the same author at the same tick collapses to ONE assertion (§6.6 dedup
--    key). Equal-valued facts from different authors = ONE fact, TWO
--    assertions (the 39 pairs' `name` facts).
-- S4 Metadata value typing (lossless, round-trippable): JSON string → Str
--    (except D4 retyping); integer fitting i64 → Int; other number → Float
--    (canonical) or BigInt (u64 > i64::MAX); bool → Term($true/$false, 0
--    args); null → Term($null, 0 args); object/array → Term($json, [Str(
--    serde canonical text)]). Today's attr path DROPS non-scalars
--    (json_scalar_to_string) — the converter must NOT (C1 losslessness).
-- S5 Blob copies of column-authoritative keys (name/file/semantic_id inside
--    the metadata blob) are SKIPPED with a counter — the COLUMN_META_KEYS
--    precedent (facts/lsm.rs:109, ledger round-008 R2): emitting them would
--    mint the same fid twice (values agree) or a phantom fact (differ).
-- S6 Defensive predicate-name collision guard: a metadata key equal to a
--    reserved/core predicate name (sid/type/name/file/span/conflict/
--    supersedes) or to an edge_type name gets predicate name "$meta:"+key
--    (reader strips the prefix on reassembly; counter in report, EXPECTED 0
--    on the real base — preds.py measured 141 DISTINCT with no collision).
-- S7 Durable conflict/5 assertion fields: author = "$rofl-convert" (the
--    converter is the asserting agent; interned like any author), tick = the
--    winner's tick (matches the OQ-1 column and keeps audit facts inside the
--    converted tick horizon), perspective = audit, Bool tag.
-- S8 provenance() tolerance carried verbatim; a NON-parseable non-missing
--    _generation value (not u64-number, not u64-numeric-string) maps to tick
--    0 and is COUNTED (unparseable_generation, expected 0) — same for a non-
--    string _source (counted, expected 0). C1 comparison normalizes BOTH
--    sides through the same §10.1 mapping: _source/_generation are compared
--    as (author, tick) — i.e. "_generation":"9" (string) and 9 (number) are
--    the same assertion, and tick 0 round-trips as ABSENT _generation
--    (measured domains never contain an explicit 0). Everything else in the
--    record (id, semantic_id, node_type, name, file, content_hash,
--    non-reserved metadata as parsed JSON values) compares EXACTLY.
--
